            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "How long do cosmetic dental results last?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "It depends on the procedure and how well you care for them. Porcelain veneers typically last 15 to 20 years or longer. Bonding lasts 5 to 10 years. Teeth whitening results fade over time and may need touch-ups every few years. Proper oral hygiene, avoiding hard foods, and addressing bite issues extend the lifespan of any cosmetic work."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Is cosmetic dentistry covered by insurance?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Most cosmetic procedures are not covered by dental insurance because they're considered elective. However, if a procedure is partly restorative (like a crown that fixes a broken tooth and improves appearance), insurance may cover a portion. We'll help you understand what's covered and provide financing options if needed."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "How do I choose between veneers and bonding?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "It varies widely depending on what's involved. A single veneer is very different from a full smile transformation with veneers, crowns, and gum contouring. We provide a detailed estimate during your consultation once we understand your goals and evaluate your case."
              }
            }
          ]
